grh-ch2-body =
  grh-ln "  <p>A central hazard of massive tactic-compacted archives—explicitly noted in <code>lsernau/grh-lean</code>&#x27;s README (<em>&ldquo;No mathematician has read it through, and no paper comes with it&rdquo;</em>)—is loss of the global relational architecture. In <code>lib/math/grh-atlas.hypercubical</code>, every space constructed across both 2026 proofs is typed explicitly in <code>data GrhSpace : Type</code> and connected by 13 intra-proof morphisms plus the 4-component unitary equivalence <code>ga-adelic-seesaw-knot : GnKnot AlpoLocalCoord MasulloLayer5Coord</code>:</p>" (
  grh-ln "  <ul>" (
  grh-ln "    <li><strong>Alp&ouml;ge&ndash;Sernau Unitary Theta-Seesaw Spaces (<code>A01</code>&ndash;<code>A11</code>, <code>grh/GUIDE.md</code>):</strong> Given modulus <span class='m'><i>N</i><sub>0</sub></span>, imaginary quadratic field <span class='m'><i>K</i> = &Qopf;(&radic;&minus;<i>d</i>)</span>, cyclotomic CM extension <span class='m'><i>E</i> = <i>K</i>(&zeta;<sub><i>N</i><sub>1</sub></sub>)</span>, and chain parameters <span class='m'><i>m</i> = 2&varrho; + 2</span>, <span class='m'><i>r</i> = <i>k</i> + <i>m</i> &minus; 1</span>, <span class='m'><i>t</i> = 5<i>r</i></span>, the proof constructs two parallel <span class='m'><i>m</i></span>-step unitary theta towers: an upper definite chain <span class='m'><i>U</i>(<i>X</i><sub>0</sub>)<sub><i>k</i></sub> &rarr; &cdots; &rarr; <i>U</i>(<i>X</i><sub><i>m</i></sub>)<sub><i>r</i>+<i>mt</i>+1</sub></span> and a lower indefinite chain <span class='m'><i>U</i>(<i>Y</i><sub>0</sub>)<sub><i>r</i></sub> &rarr; &cdots; &rarr; <i>U</i>(<i>Y</i><sub><i>m</i></sub>)<sub><i>r</i>+<i>mt</i></sub></span>, coupled through Labesse sign-swapped <span class='m'><i>U</i>(<i>W</i><sub><i>j</i></sub>)<sub><i>r</i></sub></span>, the <span class='m'><i>m</i><sup>2</sup></span>-turn Rallis/Siegel&ndash;Weil grid <span class='m'><i>U</i>(<i>V</i><sub><i>j</i></sub>)<sub><i>r</i>+<i>t</i></sub></span>, Hurwitz CM formal-group jets (<strong>Theorem A</strong>), Flensted-Jensen Bessel/Kloosterman 2nd-moment sieving (<strong>Theorem B</strong>), Shimura/Ribet/Kisin Selmer cuts, and Bost&#x27;s <code>TwistedLattice</code> slope bound (<strong>Theorem C</strong>).</li>" (
  grh-ln "    <li><strong>Masullo Adelic Nuclear LF Trace Spaces (<code>M01</code>&ndash;<code>M06</code>, <code>mccorvie/riemann-masullo</code>):</strong> Polar-killing nuclear Montel LF Schwartz space <span class='m'><i>B</i><sub>0</sub>(&Aopf;<sub><i>F</i></sub>)</span>, strict LF second-quantized theta distribution <span class='m'>&Theta;<sub><i>S</i></sub></span>, critical-strip Markushevich nuclear trace basis, divisorial Paley&ndash;Wiener prime shells, and exterior-zero trace subtraction forcing all nontrivial Hecke zeros onto <span class='m'>&Re;(&rho;) = 1/2</span>.</li>" (
  grh-ln "  </ul>" (
  grh-ln "  <div class='eq-box'>" (
  grh-ln "    <span class='m'><i>m</i> = 2&varrho; + 2, &emsp; <i>r</i> = <i>k</i> + <i>m</i> &minus; 1, &emsp; <i>t</i> = 5<i>r</i> &ensp;&rArr;&ensp; rank(<i>X</i><sub><i>m</i></sub>) &minus; rank(<i>Y</i><sub><i>m</i></sub>) = [<i>k</i> + <i>m</i>(<i>t</i> + 1)] &minus; [<i>r</i> + <i>mt</i>] &equiv; 1</span>" (
  grh-ln "    <span class='eq-sub'>Certified universally over &Zopf;[k, &varrho;, j] by <code>ga-cert-space-corank1</code> (5 &rarr; 0 muls, <code>refl</code>): <i>Y<sub>m</sub> &sub; X<sub>m</sub></i> has exact co-rank 1 for every (k, &varrho;)!</span>" (
  grh-ln "  </div>" (
  grh-ln "  <div class='lab-card' id='labAtlas'>" (
  grh-ln "    <div class='lab-head'>" (
  grh-ln "      <span class='lbl'>Lab 1 &middot; Interactive 17-Space Unitary&ndash;Adelic Atlas &amp; Co-Rank-1 Seesaw Explorer</span>" (
  grh-ln "      <span class='lab-status' id='atlasStatus'>17 Spaces &middot; 13 Morphisms &middot; 4 GnKnot Regularizer Bridges</span>" (
  grh-ln "    </div>" (
  grh-ln "    <div class='lab-ctrl'>" (
  grh-ln "      <button class='lab-btn on' data-af='all' type='button'>All 17 Spaces</button>" (
  grh-ln "      <button class='lab-btn' data-af='alpo' type='button'>Alp&ouml;ge Seesaw (A01&ndash;A11)</button>" (
